{"_doc":"Hand-written source for scripts/build_words.py. Invariable words and set phrases (no gender, plural or possessive forms), in arabizi with the Arabic spelling. group: time (when), calendar (units, days, seasons, this/next/last), direction (left, right, compass, here/there, where), weather (weather and temperature phrases). kind: word or phrase. None of these are from the Peace Corps book; the author wrote them, so they should be checked with a speaker.",
"words":[
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"l-yum","ar":"اليوم","en":"today","ex":{"lat":"ghadi nkhdem l-yum","ar":"غادي نخدم اليوم","en":"Today I am going to work"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"l-bare7","ar":"البارح","en":"yesterday","ex":{"lat":"mchit l s-suq l-bare7","ar":"مشيت للسوق البارح","en":"Yesterday I went to the market"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"ghedda","ar":"غدا","en":"tomorrow","ex":{"lat":"ghadi nchufek ghedda","ar":"غادي نشوفك غدا","en":"Tomorrow I will see you"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"b3d ghedda","ar":"بعد غدا","en":"the day after tomorrow"},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"daba","ar":"دابا","en":"now","ex":{"lat":"kankhdem daba","ar":"كنخدم دابا","en":"Now I am working"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"dghya","ar":"دغيا","en":"quickly / right away","note":"Also used for soon: nji dghya, I will come soon."},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"men b3d","ar":"من بعد","en":"later / afterwards","ex":{"lat":"nchufu men b3d","ar":"نشوفو من بعد","en":"We will see each other later"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"dima","ar":"ديما","en":"always","ex":{"lat":"huwa dima kaytsennak","ar":"هو ديما كيتسناك","en":"He always waits for you"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"bekri","ar":"بكري","en":"early","ex":{"lat":"kanfiq bekri","ar":"كنفيق بكري","en":"I wake up early"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"mazal","ar":"مازال","en":"still / not yet","note":"With a verb it means still (mazal kaykhdem, he is still working). With ma and a negative it means not yet."},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"s-sba7","ar":"الصباح","en":"morning","note":"s-sba7 on its own also means in the morning."},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"z-zwal","ar":"الزوال","en":"noon / midday"},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"l-3chiya","ar":"العشية","en":"afternoon / evening","note":"The late afternoon into the evening, after about 4 pm."},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"l-lil","ar":"الليل","en":"night","note":"l-lil is the night as a time of day; lila is one night (lila wa7da)."},
  {"group":"time","kind":"word","lat":"nus l-lil","ar":"نص الليل","en":"midnight"},
  {"group":"time","kind":"phrase","lat":"imta?","ar":"إمتا؟","en":"when?","ex":{"lat":"imta ghadi tji?","ar":"إمتا غادي تجي؟","en":"When are you coming?"}},
  {"group":"time","kind":"phrase","lat":"kul nhar","ar":"كل نهار","en":"every day","note":"kul + a noun means every: kul semmana, kul chher, kul 3am."},

  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"tanya","ar":"تانية","en":"second (of time)"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"dqiqa","ar":"دقيقة","en":"minute"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"sa3a","ar":"ساعة","en":"hour / o'clock","note":"Also asks the time: ch7al f s-sa3a?"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"nhar","ar":"نهار","en":"day","note":"Masculine. Also the daytime. For a calendar day yum is understood too."},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"semmana","ar":"سيمانة","en":"week"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"chher","ar":"شهر","en":"month"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"3am","ar":"عام","en":"year","note":"sna (a school or fiscal year, and the way you count age) is also heard."},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"t-tnin","ar":"التنين","en":"Monday","note":"Often nhar t-tnin. The days: t-tnin, t-tlata, l-arb3a, l-khmis, j-jem3a, s-sebt, l-7ed."},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"t-tlata","ar":"التلاتا","en":"Tuesday"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"l-arb3a","ar":"لاربعا","en":"Wednesday"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"l-khmis","ar":"الخميس","en":"Thursday"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"j-jem3a","ar":"الجمعة","en":"Friday","note":"The day of the main prayer. Many shops and offices close for part of it."},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"s-sebt","ar":"السبت","en":"Saturday"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"l-7ed","ar":"الحد","en":"Sunday"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"ch-chta","ar":"الشتا","en":"winter","note":"ch-chta also means the rain."},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"r-rbi3","ar":"الربيع","en":"spring"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"s-sif","ar":"الصيف","en":"summer"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"word","lat":"l-khrif","ar":"الخريف","en":"autumn"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"had s-semmana","ar":"هاد السيمانة","en":"this week","note":"had + the noun with its article: this. Feminine nouns (semmana) take jaya and fatet; masculine ones (chher, 3am) take jay and fat."},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"s-semmana jaya","ar":"السيمانة الجاية","en":"next week"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"s-semmana lli fatet","ar":"السيمانة اللي فاتت","en":"last week"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"had ch-chher","ar":"هاد الشهر","en":"this month"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"ch-chher jay","ar":"الشهر الجاي","en":"next month"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"ch-chher lli fat","ar":"الشهر اللي فات","en":"last month"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"had l-3am","ar":"هاد العام","en":"this year"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"l-3am jay","ar":"العام الجاي","en":"next year"},
  {"group":"calendar","kind":"phrase","lat":"l-3am lli fat","ar":"العام اللي فات","en":"last year"},

  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"limen","ar":"ليمن","en":"right","note":"As a direction: 3la limen, to the right."},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"liser","ar":"ليسر","en":"left","note":"As a direction: 3la liser, to the left."},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"nichan","ar":"نيشان","en":"straight ahead","note":"dghri is also used."},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"chmal","ar":"شمال","en":"north"},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"janub","ar":"جنوب","en":"south"},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"charq","ar":"شرق","en":"east"},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"gharb","ar":"غرب","en":"west"},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"hna","ar":"هنا","en":"here","ex":{"lat":"gles hna","ar":"ڭلس هنا","en":"Sit here"}},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"temma","ar":"تما","en":"there","ex":{"lat":"d-dar dyali temma","ar":"الدار ديالي تما","en":"My house is there"}},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"word","lat":"fin","ar":"فين","en":"where","note":"fin kayn...? is where is...? mnin means from where; l-fin means to where."},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"phrase","lat":"fin kayn l-benka?","ar":"فين كاين البنكة؟","en":"where is the bank?","note":"kayn means there is, so this is literally where is there the bank."},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"phrase","lat":"dwer 3la limen","ar":"دور على ليمن","en":"turn right"},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"phrase","lat":"dwer 3la liser","ar":"دور على ليسر","en":"turn left"},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"phrase","lat":"mchi nichan","ar":"مشي نيشان","en":"go straight"},
  {"group":"direction","kind":"phrase","lat":"7bes hna","ar":"حبس هنا","en":"stop here","note":"What you tell a taxi driver."},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"word","lat":"l-fsul","ar":"الفصول","en":"the seasons","note":"The four are ch-chta (winter), r-rbi3 (spring), s-sif (summer), l-khrif (autumn).","ex":{"lat":"kaynin rb3a d l-fsul f l-3am","ar":"كاينين ربعة د الفصول فالعام","en":"There are four seasons in a year"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"word","lat":"l-jaw","ar":"الجو","en":"the weather","ex":{"lat":"kifach l-jaw l-yum?","ar":"كيفاش الجو اليوم؟","en":"How is the weather today?"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"l-jaw zwin","ar":"الجو زوين","en":"nice weather","note":"Two patterns: j-jaw plus an adjective (j-jaw zwin, j-jaw bard), or kayn / kayna plus a noun: kayn with masculine nouns (kayn r-rih), kayna with feminine ones (kayna ch-chta).","ex":{"lat":"l-jaw zwin, bghit nmchi l l-ba7r","ar":"الجو زوين، بغيت نمشي للبحر","en":"The weather is nice, I want to go to the beach"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"l-jaw khayb","ar":"الجو خايب","en":"bad weather","ex":{"lat":"l-jaw khayb, ma ghadich nkhrej","ar":"الجو خايب، ما غاديش نخرج","en":"The weather is bad, I am not going out"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"l-jaw bared","ar":"الجو بارد","en":"cold weather","ex":{"lat":"l-jaw bared f ch-chta","ar":"الجو بارد فالشتا","en":"The weather is cold in winter"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"l-jaw skhoun","ar":"الجو سخون","en":"hot weather","ex":{"lat":"l-jaw skhoun f s-sif","ar":"الجو سخون فالصيف","en":"The weather is hot in summer"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayn l-bard","ar":"كاين البرد","en":"it's cold","note":"l-bard (البرد) is the cold itself; bard (بارد) is the adjective: j-jaw bard.","ex":{"lat":"kayn l-bard bzzaf had s-sba7","ar":"كاين البرد بزاف هاد الصباح","en":"It is very cold this morning"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna ch-chems","ar":"كاينة الشمس","en":"it's sunny","ex":{"lat":"kayna ch-chems l-yum","ar":"كاينة الشمس اليوم","en":"It is sunny today"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"l-jaw mghayem","ar":"الجو مغيم","en":"it's cloudy","ex":{"lat":"l-jaw mghayem w ghadi tji ch-chta","ar":"الجو مغيم وغادي تجي الشتا","en":"It is cloudy and it is going to rain"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayn r-rih","ar":"كاين الريح","en":"it's windy","ex":{"lat":"kayn r-rih bezzaf l-yum","ar":"كاين الريح بزاف اليوم","en":"It is very windy today"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna ch-chta","ar":"كاينة الشتا","en":"it's raining","note":"ch-chta is both the rain and the winter.","ex":{"lat":"kayna ch-chta, khod l-mdella","ar":"كاينة الشتا، خود المظلة","en":"It is raining, take the umbrella"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayn t-talj","ar":"كاين التلج","en":"there's snow","ex":{"lat":"kayn t-talj f l-atlas","ar":"كاين التلج فالأطلس","en":"There is snow in the Atlas"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayn r-r3d","ar":"كاين الرعد","en":"there's thunder","ex":{"lat":"sme3t r-r3d l-bare7","ar":"سمعت الرعد البارح","en":"I heard the thunder yesterday"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayn l-berq","ar":"كاين البرق","en":"there's lightning","ex":{"lat":"chft l-berq f s-sma","ar":"شفت البرق فالسما","en":"I saw lightning in the sky"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna 3asifa","ar":"كاينة عاصفة","en":"there's a storm","ex":{"lat":"kayna 3asifa, ma tkhrejch","ar":"كاينة عاصفة، ما تخرجش","en":"There is a storm, do not go out"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayn s-sahd","ar":"كاين السهد","en":"it's scorching","note":"A spell of very hot, dry weather.","ex":{"lat":"kayn s-sahd had s-semmana","ar":"كاين السهد هاد السيمانة","en":"It is scorching this week"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna d-dbaba","ar":"كاينة الضبابة","en":"it's foggy","ex":{"lat":"kayna d-dbaba f s-sba7","ar":"كاينة الضبابة فالصباح","en":"There is fog in the morning"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"word","lat":"l-7arara","ar":"الحرارة","en":"the heat","ex":{"lat":"l-7arara tal3a bezzaf f s-sif","ar":"الحرارة طالعة بزاف فالصيف","en":"It gets very hot in summer"},"note":"Also the word for a fever or temperature."},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayn ch-chergui","ar":"كاين الشرقي","en":"the chergui is blowing","note":"The chergui is the hot, dry wind from the east.","ex":{"lat":"kayn ch-chergui l-yum, l-jaw skhoun","ar":"كاين الشرقي اليوم، الجو سخون","en":"The chergui is blowing today, the weather is hot"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna r-rtuba","ar":"كاينة الرطوبة","en":"it's humid","ex":{"lat":"f Casa kayna r-rtuba bezzaf","ar":"فكازا كاينة الرطوبة بزاف","en":"In Casa there is a lot of humidity"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"s-sma safya","ar":"السما صافية","en":"clear sky","ex":{"lat":"s-sma safya l-yum","ar":"السما صافية اليوم","en":"The sky is clear today"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna chta qwiya","ar":"كاينة شتا قوية","en":"there's heavy rain","ex":{"lat":"kayna chta qwiya f l-lil","ar":"كاينة شتا قوية فالليل","en":"There is heavy rain at night"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna chta khfifa","ar":"كاينة شتا خفيفة","en":"there's light rain","ex":{"lat":"kayna chta khfifa f s-sba7","ar":"كاينة شتا خفيفة فالصباح","en":"There is light rain in the morning"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"kayna s-skhana","ar":"كاينة السخانة","en":"it's hot","note":"s-skhana is the heat; skhun is the adjective: j-jaw skhun.","ex":{"lat":"kayna s-skhana bezzaf had s-semmana","ar":"كاينة السخانة بزاف هاد السيمانة","en":"It is very hot this week"}},
  {"group":"weather","kind":"phrase","lat":"katchti","ar":"كتشتي","en":"it's raining","note":"The most common way to say it: the verb chta, yechti. Also d-denya katchti.","ex":{"lat":"katchti l-yum, khod l-mdella","ar":"كتشتي اليوم، خود المظلة","en":"It is raining today, take the umbrella"}}
]}
